Myself and others have also had issues with integrating Telemetry data with secr, particularly with multisession data.  Here are some other folks that have asked similar questions.

https://groups.google.com/forum/#!searchin/secrgroup/nathan%7Csort:date/secrgroup/jXUqznWyGWQ/uQKe7afXCAAJ

https://groups.google.com/forum/#!searchin/secrgroup/nathan%7Csort:date/secrgroup/G2Vcq3Jo7PE/YYIzf8KYAgAJ

The second link addresses your occasion question.  I have gotten passed issues with ocassions in telemetry data by setting them all to 1 since telemetry occasion is rarely used in secr models

Ultimately if you cannot figure out how to solve your problems secr, there is also the option of migrating over to oscr. That is what had to do. The data management is way more involved with oscr ( requires a solid understanding of data tables and matrices in r)  but the developers are super responsive and helpful.

Best,

David

