Yes, that sounds right to me. I don't know what happens in general if you continue to increase the buffer far beyond the point where sigma is identifiable, e.g. will the point estimates stabilize like you're seeing. Perhaps so. I believe if you convert the 20km sigma estimate to a 95% home range area, it will be much larger than that expected for a wolverine and also much larger than the trapping array area (though I can't infer the dimensions from the info in these emails), suggesting the 20km estimate is due to a trapping array that is too small for Mb.

Ben

