Hi -

Murray, I looked into this a bit more. For 2 of the individuals, all of the re-detections occurred at the initial site. For the 5 remaining, it was a bit more mixed, but even then 2 of them had almost all of their re-detections at the initial site. So, yes, I would have to agree that the informative dataset is indeed pretty thin.

Ben to your point, a sigma of ~20km translates to an estimated home range of ~7500 km^2 which is indeed much larger than a wolverine home range as well as the trapping array - supporting what you've written that the estimate is due to a trapping array too small for Mb.

Thank you both. I really appreciate your help sorting through this.

Andrea

